Version 4.2, fall 1984.
First Adventure game written by His Lordship, the honorable
Admiral D.W. Riggle

You are the Great wizard ken.

	This is a luxurious stateroom.
The floor is carpeted with a soft animal fur and the great wooden furniture
is inlaid with strips of platinum and gold.  Electronic equipment built
into the walls and ceiling is flashing wildly.  The floor shudders and
the sounds of dull explosions rumble though the room.  From a window in
the wall ahead comes a view of darkest space.  There is a small adjoining
room behind you, and a doorway right.

>-: two-handed sword:
Zap! Taken from thin air.
>-: 
Room (was 22) = Time (was 1) = Fuel (was 250) = Torps (was 10) = CUMBER (was 10) = WEIGHT (was 60) = Clock (was 120) = Wizard (was 1, 0) = 
DONE.
There is a fierce woodsman here brandishing a heavy mallet.
<fight!>-: You smite him to the ground.
But in a flurry of steel he regains his feet!
He attacks...
I'm afraid you have suffered some minor lacerations.
<fight!>-: His ribs crack under your powerful swing, flooding his lungs with blood.
You have killed the Woodsman.

	The road crosses the lagoon here.
Coursing through the trees, the road at this point bridges a watery finger
of the lagoon. The water is behind you. The road continues right and left.

A dead woodsman has fallen here. He was savagely murdered.
A heavy wooden mallet lies nearby.
>-: Your two-handed sword should do the trick.
You can't kill the two-handed sword!
